.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# ---- generated output (never commit; rebuild from the sources) -------------
# The maker skill writes its diagrams here. Nothing links to them, and they are
# regenerable: skills/maker/render.py -o out/<name>
/out/

# skill-publish's build tree (tools/skill-publish/build-index.py --dist default).
# It is a copy of skills/ plus a generated index.json, so committing it would
# publish a second, stale set of skills from a path nothing serves.
/tools/skill-publish/dist/

# ---- local working copies of source material (never commit) ----------------
# These hold large source media that must stay on disk but do not belong in git:
#   Photos/   raw instructor photos and phone video (the site uses the resized,
#             EXIF-stripped copies under assets/photos/class/)
#   slides/   source .pptx class decks (the committed artifact is the built PDF
#             + slides.html, per the deck-sync rule in AGENTS.md)
#   videos/   legacy full-desktop screen recordings, used as teaching source for
#             tools/video-build/ projects; cannot be re-edited into the new look
#             (see make-legacy-tips.py)
#
# Leading slash anchors these to the repo root. Do not drop it: an unanchored
# Photos/ would also match assets/photos/ on a case-insensitive filesystem.
/Photos/
/slides/
/videos/

# ---- video-build render intermediates (never commit) -----------------------
# The pipeline keeps recordings, narration audio and render intermediates in a
# per-project workDir OUTSIDE the repo (video.json -> workDir). These rules are
# the belt to that suspenders: if a project ever omits workDir, pipeline.py
# falls back to <project>/build/ INSIDE the repo, which would otherwise stage
# hundreds of MB of media on the next `git add`.
#
# Only rendered media is excluded. The scene scripts themselves are source and
# live in tools/video-build/projects/<slug>/takes/*.js — those stay committed,
# so these patterns must match the media, not the whole directory.
tools/video-build/**/build/
tools/video-build/**/cap/
*.mov
*.wav
*.aiff
*.m4a

# ---- site-nav render probes (never commit) ---------------------------------
# verify-render.py injects a probe into each page and writes it to the repo root
# so the page's relative asset paths still resolve. It removes each one, but an
# interrupted run would otherwise leave a page copy staged for publishing.
/.render-probe-*.html
